<h2 id="bring-your-schedule-into-helium">Bring Your Schedule into Helium</h2>

<p>
  The fastest way to get an existing schedule into Helium is the <strong>AI-assisted import</strong>. You hand your
  source material to any modern AI assistant, it produces a Helium import file, and you upload that file to Helium.
</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    Follow the <a href="/support/getting-started/where-to-start-with-helium/#import-a-whole-syllabus-with-ai"><strong>AI-assisted syllabus import</strong></a> steps in <em>Where to Start with Helium</em>.
  </li>
  <li>
    When the assistant asks for your source material, attach the <strong><code>.ics</code> file</strong> you saved above — or simply paste your list of classes, meeting times, and assignments.
  </li>
  <li>
    Answer its follow-up questions, download the import file it produces, and import it under <a href="https://app.heliumedu.com/settings/import-export"><strong>Settings → Import / Export</strong></a>.
  </li>
</ol>

<p>
  Prefer to set things up by hand? The <a href="/support/getting-started/where-to-start-with-helium/#set-up-your-first-term"><strong>manual walkthrough</strong></a> in the same article gets you to a usable term step by step. See <a href="/support/import-export-and-backup/importing-and-exporting-your-data/">Importing &amp; Exporting Your Data</a> for how Helium's import works.
</p>

<blockquote>
  <p><strong>Note:</strong> Helium is free and open source, including cross-device sync. To see what Helium does, <a href="https://www.heliumedu.com/#features">check out our homepage</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
